  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of resilience and livelihood through food for training and food for asset activities in Sa&#x2019;adah governorate</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide food assistance to vulnerable communities affected by displacement and disrupted agriculture. This WFP project provides assistance to 900 households (6,300 beneficiaries) with the objective of helping the households build skills for livelihood, and also aims to target as much as possible the households whose members are Pregnant and Lactating Women and Girls (PLWG) as well as vulnerable HHs in the communities. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 5,418 people, including 1,432 women, 1,471 men, 2,515 children, and including 945 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
